This method takes a file and a list of time ranges as input, and returns a list of thread snapshots that are within the given time ranges. It uses a BufferedReader to read the contents of the file line by line, and then checks each line against the time ranges in the list, and adds a new ThreadSnapshot object with the appropriate status, startTime, endTime, and stackTrace if the line is within one of the time ranges. The method throws an IllegalArgumentException if either the file or the timeRanges list is null, or if a line does not have a valid time range.

public static List<ThreadSnapshot> parseFromFileWithTimeRange(File file, List<ProfileAnalyzeTimeRange> timeRanges) throws IOException {
    // Create a new ArrayList to store the parsed thread snapshots
    List<ThreadSnapshot> threadSnapshots = new ArrayList<>();

    // Create a new BufferedReader to read the contents of the file
    BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(file));

    // Read each line of the file, and if it is a valid ThreadSnapshot, add it to the list
    String line;
    while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
        try {
            ThreadSnapshot threadSnapshot = ThreadSnapshot.parseFromLine(line);
            if (timeRanges.contains(threadSnapshot.getTimeRange())) {
                threadSnapshots.add(threadSnapshot);
            }
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
            // Ignore invalid lines
        }
    }

    // Close the reader and return the list of parsed thread snapshots
    reader.close();
    return threadSnapshots;
}
